Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: arm64: dts: allwinner: orangepi-zero2/zero3: add Mali-G31 OPP table for devfreq

Include the H616/H618 GPU operating points (dt_64/sun50i-h616-gpu-opp.dtsi,
306-600 MHz at 810-950 mV, already used by the KickPi K2B boards) from the
DTSI shared by the Orange Pi Zero2 and Zero3, so panfrost registers a
devfreq device and scales the Mali-G31 clock/voltage with load instead of
running at a fixed clock.

Both boards power the GPU from a "vdd-gpu-sys" regulator whose range in the
board DTS is 810000-990000 uV (Zero2: AXP305 reg_dcdcc, Zero3: AXP313a
reg_dcdc1), so every OPP target voltage (810-950 mV) and the 990 mV ceiling
fit inside the regulator constraints.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
  */
 
 #include "sun50i-h616.dtsi"
+#include "sun50i-h616-gpu-opp.dtsi"
 
 #include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/arm-gic.h>
